      "id": "2048087004106395864",
      "text": "most founders treat marketing like a chore they'll get to later.\n\nlater never comes.\n\nyou're too deep in the product. there's always a bug to fix or a feature to ship.\n\nand then six months pass and nobody knows you exist.\n\nthe problem isn't motivation. it's that marketing as a solo founder requires four different skill sets running in parallel.\n\nseo. content. social. community.\n\nif you're good at one, you're probably ignoring the other three.\n\nokara handles all four. you just review before anything goes live.",
