      "text": "most early-stage teams don't have a marketing problem.\n\nthey have a bandwidth problem.\n\nthe founder is doing sales. the engineers are shipping. and growth just... sits there. waiting for someone to have time.\n\nso nothing gets posted. no one follows up on the content idea from two weeks ago. the distribution strategy lives in a doc nobody opens.\n\nI kept seeing this pattern great product, smart team, zero traction and the reason was almost never the product.\n\nit was that nobody owned growth consistently.\n\nthat's the actual problem we're solving at https://t.co/nPH2wroxYw.\n\nan AI CMO that keeps growth moving even when your team can't",
